   "sentenceId": 12,
   "he": "הַמּוֹתָר, רַבִּי מֵאִיר אוֹמֵר הֶקְדֵּשׁ. אֵימַת קָדוֹשׁ? רַב וּשְׁמוּאֵל דְּאָמְרִי תַּרְוַויְיהוּ: מוֹתָר לְאַחַר מִיתָה קָדוֹשׁ. רַב אַדָּא בַּר אַהֲבָה אָמַר: מוֹתָר מֵחַיִּים קָדוֹשׁ.",
   "en": "§ The mishna states that with regard to «the surplus, Rabbi Meir says: It is consecrated» property. The Gemara asks: According to this opinion, «when» does the surplus amount become «consecrated? Rav and Shmuel both said: The surplus is consecrated» only «after» the woman’s «death. Rav Adda bar Ahava said: The surplus is consecrated while» she is still «alive.»"
  }
